# Entity page pattern

Every entity page (campaigns, landers, offers, traffic sources, etc.) follows the same structure. Copy the pattern, not improvise.

## State shape
```tsx
export function ThingsPage() {
  const toast = useToastApi()
  const navigate = useNavigate()
  const tableRef = useRef<Table<ThingRow> | null>(null)

  // UI state
  const [search, setSearch] = useState('')
  const [sheetOpen, setSheetOpen] = useState(false)
  const [editId, setEditId] = useState<string | null>(null)
  const [deleteTarget, setDeleteTarget] = useState<{ id: string } | null>(null)

  // Data
  const { data: editThing } = useThing(editId ?? '')
  const saveMutation = useSaveThing()
  const deleteMutation = useDeleteThing()
  const cloneMutation = useCloneThing()
  // ...
```

## CRUD handlers
```tsx
const handleCreate = () => { setEditId(null); setSheetOpen(true) }
const handleEdit = (id: string) => { setEditId(id); setSheetOpen(true) }

const handleSubmit = (data: ThingFormData) => {
  const isNew = !data.idThing || data.idThing === '0'
  const payload: SaveThingInput = {
    ...data,
    idThing: isNew ? generateId() : data.idThing,
    create: isNew,
  }
  saveMutation.mutate(payload, {
    onSuccess: () => {
      toast.success(isNew ? 'Created' : 'Updated')
      setSheetOpen(false)
      setEditId(null)
    },
    onError: (err) => toast.error(getErrorMessage(err)),
  })
}

const handleDelete = () => {
  if (!deleteTarget) return
  deleteMutation.mutate(deleteTarget.id, {
    onSuccess: () => { toast.success('Deleted'); setDeleteTarget(null) },
    onError: (err) => toast.error(getErrorMessage(err)),
  })
}
```

## ID generation
New entities get client-generated IDs via `generateId()` from `@/lib/id-generator`. The API expects the client to provide the ID on POST (not auto-increment).

## JSX structure
```tsx
return (
  <PageShell title="Things" actions={<Button type="primary" onClick={handleCreate}>New Thing</Button>}>
    <SearchToolbar value={search} onChange={setSearch} />
    <DataTable
      data={filteredData}
      columns={columnDefs}
      tableRef={tableRef}
      // table config from useTableConfigStore
    />
    <BulkActionsBar ... />

    {/* Edit modal */}
    <ThingEditForm
      open={sheetOpen}
      onOpenChange={setSheetOpen}
      initialData={editId ? editThing : undefined}
      onSubmit={handleSubmit}
      isSubmitting={saveMutation.isPending}
    />

    {/* Delete confirmation */}
    <ConfirmModal
      open={!!deleteTarget}
      onConfirm={handleDelete}
      onCancel={() => setDeleteTarget(null)}
      title="Delete Thing"
      description="This cannot be undone."
      danger
      loading={deleteMutation.isPending}
    />
  </PageShell>
)
```

## Routing and permissions
- Route defined in `App.tsx` inside `<AppRoutes>`.
- Wrap with `guarded((p) => p.things.canView, <ThingsPage />)`.
- Edit permission check: `guarded((p) => p.things.canEdit, ...)`.

## Data filtering
Client-side search filtering:
```tsx
const filteredData = useMemo(() => {
  if (!search) return data ?? []
  const q = search.toLowerCase()
  return (data ?? []).filter((item) =>
    item.name.toLowerCase().includes(q)
  )
}, [data, search])
```

## Never
- Never put data fetching logic directly in the page — use hooks from `@/api/hooks/`.
- Never manage form state with useState — use the edit form component with RHF.
- Never show delete confirmation with `window.confirm` — use `ConfirmModal`.
- Never generate IDs on the server — use `generateId()` client-side.
- Never navigate without permission checks.
- Never forget to pass `isSubmitting` to disable the submit button during save.
